   3. Extracted the raw SSR-embedded JSON for this product's `variationAttributes` and confirmed definitively: the Search endpoint's `size` attribute values carry `{"name":..., "value":...}` only — **no `orderable` field at all** on any value. This proves `selectSizeChipValues`'s `isDisabled: value.orderable === false` logic is correctly written but structurally can never be `true` on PLP today, because the underlying Search endpoint data it reads from doesn't carry per-size orderable information (unlike the Product Detail/`getProducts` endpoint, confirmed earlier in the session to have this field).
