// Fixed 2026-09-10, closing a real, live-confirmed bug (Figma-vs-build audit, Marcel); corrected
// again same day once the fix below was itself found to cancel the wrong padding source. The
// negative-margin trick that lets a `RecommendedProducts` rail bleed edge-to-edge (PDP's Complete-
// the-Set/Might-Also-Like/Recently-Viewed via `PageContainer boxed={true}`, PLP's Recently-Viewed
// via root `layerStyle="page"`) previously used plain Chakra numeric spacing
// (`{base: -4, md: -8, lg: 0}`, i.e. -16px/-32px/0) with no named source at all. The first fix
// re-derived it from `theme/foundation/gridSystem.ts`'s `grid.containerPadding` — correct-looking,
// but that token set is for the header/footer/grid system, not this container: PDP's
// `PageContainer` (`overrides/app/components/pageContainer/index.tsx`) and PLP's `layerStyle="page"`
// both resolve to the *base* SFCC theme's own long-standing, un-migrated padding scale instead —
// confirmed byte-identical between `pageContainer/index.tsx`'s own `paddingXValue` and
// `node_modules/@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/theme/foundations/layerStyles.js`'s `page.px`:
// `[4, 4, 6, 6, 8]` (16/16/24/24/32px at base/sm/md/lg/xl). Cancelling `gridSystem.ts`'s
// 32/32/32/32/40px against that real 16/16/24/24/32px scale left every breakpoint mismatched — the
// rail still wasn't flush. `[4, 4, 6, 6, 8]` in Chakra's numeric scale happens to equal
// `[m, m, xl, xl, 2xl]` in Zimmermann's own named scale (`spacing.ts`: m=16px, xl=24px, 2xl=32px),
// so this cancels the *real* ambient padding while still only referencing registered
// `--zimm-scale-*` tokens, never a hand-typed number. Three steps, not two, since the real scale
// genuinely changes value at md (24px) before reaching xl (32px) — collapsing md/lg into one step
// and base/sm into another still matches `[4,4,6,6,8]`'s own repeated-value pattern exactly.
export const PAGE_CONTENT_BLEED_MX = {
  base: 'calc(var(--zimm-scale-m) * -1)',
  md: 'calc(var(--zimm-scale-xl) * -1)',
  xl: 'calc(var(--zimm-scale-2xl) * -1)',
} as const;

